# Migration files are hashed into supabase_migrations.schema_migration_files when applied.
# That hash is only meaningful if the bytes are the same in every checkout: with core.autocrlf=true
# a Windows working tree would hold CRLF, a Linux runner LF, and `migrate verify` would report nine
# applied files as "changed after it was applied" purely from line endings. eol=lf makes the
# checkout deterministic; existing files are renormalised in the same change.
supabase/migrations/*.sql text eol=lf
